"""Recursive subgoal controller for ``mini_prover``.

This module owns the proof-shaping loop that would otherwise make
``mini_prover.py`` sprawl: decompose the root into decisive helper claims,
compile them against the root context, prove each helper as its own Lean goal,
and try to close the root after every accepted helper.  Model I/O and Lean
checks stay answer-safe: the caller supplies the prompt-visible preamble, and
hidden PutnamBench answer definitions never enter this controller.
"""

